:0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- `nvim --version`: NVIM 0.1.5\n- Vim (version: 7.4) behaves differently? Yes\n- Operating system/version: arch 4.7.1-1-ARCH\n- Terminal name/version: st 0.6\n- `$TERM`: st-256color\n### Actual behaviour\n\nWhen `laststatus == 0` and `splitbelow` is set with the opening of every horizontal split nvim decreases the total winheight decreases by one.\nBasically, with every toggle of an horizontal window, vim eats a line, which is very annoying.\n### Expected behaviour\n\nInitially we have a window, with height, say `h_prev`, if we do an horizontal split with `:split` and then close it, the new height, say `h_new`, is such that, `h_new = h_prev - 1`\n### Steps to reproduce using `nvim -u NORC`\n\n```\nnvim -u NORC             # fire up nvim\n:set splitbelow\n:set laststatus=0\n:echo winheight ('%')    # annotate this value: 'h_prev'\n:split\n:q\n:echo winheight ('%')    # annotate this value: 'h_new'\n```\n\nObserve that `h_new = h_prev - 1`\n","closed_by":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_typ